√vyath (vyáthate; vivyathé [785];
ávyathiṣṭa; vyathitá).
 —1. move to
and fro, rock, reel;
 —2. fig. (like Eng. be
restless) be disturbed in mind, be pained.

vyāpāra, m.
 —1. business, i. e. occupation;
 —2. (as in Eng.) business, i. e. concern,
 30^4;
 —3. activity, exertion. [√3pṛ
+ vy-ā, ‘be busied.’]
